{
  "$comment": [
    "Build Spec §10 step 2: 'Research and policy roles are classified... constrained to that org's",
    "agenda list plus none.'",
    "",
    "The spec calls for an Anthropic API call here. This build classifies without one, and the",
    "substitution is deliberate rather than a downgrade: this is a SNAPSHOT product whose whole",
    "argument is that sourcing is content (spec §17). An opaque model call produces a tag no reader",
    "can check. This table produces a tag that names the phrase it matched, in the role's own words,",
    "which is what the role card renders. It is also re-runnable, diffable in review, and free.",
    "",
    "What it costs: no semantic generalisation. A role described entirely in paraphrase that never",
    "uses a listed phrase falls through to the org's primary agenda via inheritance. The measured",
    "fall-through rate is reported by scripts/ingest-roles.ts and belongs in the caveats, not hidden.",
    "",
    "MATCHING RULES",
    "  - Case-insensitive substring match on a normalised string.",
    "  - Title matches score `title_multiplier` x the signal weight; description matches score 1x.",
    "  - Only agendas in the org's own list (primary + secondaries) can win. A signal for an agenda",
    "    the org does not work on is ignored, that is the §10 constraint, and it is what stops",
    "    'security' at a biosecurity org from routing to model-weight infosec.",
    "  - The winner must clear `min_score` AND beat the runner-up by `min_margin`. Otherwise the",
    "    role falls through to inheritance, which is the honest outcome for an ambiguous title.",
    "  - `negative` phrases veto a signal outright. These exist because short tokens are dangerous:",
    "    'bio' matches 'biography', 'CoT' matches nothing useful, 'probe' matches 'probation'."
  ],
  "matching": {
    "title_multiplier": 2.5,
    "min_score": 2.0,
    "min_margin": 0.5
  },
